{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Message Bus Architecture"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use to talk about the message bus architecture. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Build the application installation program, using IT development tools available in the market, based on solution architecture features.   Recognizes and implements the different types of architecture styles that can be included in the IT solution."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.   Exchanges simple information on the hardware devices and the architecture of a system to create the IT solution."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Conditional Sentences With If Clauses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>You use <strong>conditionals </strong>with<strong> if clauses </strong>to express that a cause in the present has consequence in the future.</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you use a message bus, you will reduce complexity in application communication."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p><strong>Conditionals </strong>have two sentences that express a cause, represented by the conjunction <strong><i>if </i></strong>plus an action in present, and a consequence which in this case is going to be represented by the future <strong>will.</strong></p> <p>The clause with <strong>if </strong>can be the first or the second sentence. Regardless the order, the meaning will be the same. Look at these two grammatical structures:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>If </strong>+ subject + <strong>verb in present</strong> + complement + <strong>(,) </strong>+ subject + <strong>will </strong>+ complement.</p> <p style=\"text-align: left;\">Example<i>:</i></p> <p><strong><i>If</i></strong><i> we <strong>use</strong> the message bus architecture<strong>,</strong> we <strong>will </strong>connect diverse application at the same time. &nbsp;</i></p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Subject + <strong>will</strong> + complement + <strong>if</strong> + subject + <strong>verb in present</strong> + complement</p> <p>Example:</p> <p><i>We <strong>will </strong>connect diverse application at the same time <strong>If</strong> we <strong>use</strong> the message bus architecture. </i></p> <p>Notice that in the previous example, we omitted the comma because the <strong>if clause</strong> was placed as the second sentence.</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I link all the applications, there will be many point-to-point connections. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If various components or services need to interact, they will use a message bus."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Message Bus Architecture"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "This architecture style allows users to connect more than one application on a computing platform. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>When we talk about the <strong>message bus architecture style</strong>, we must take into account that it is a software designed to bind computational, data, display, or graphic services, as well as program interpreters. All these services are able to communicate by using the bus; therefore, sharing data is a flexible process.</p> <p>The word <strong>bus</strong> is used to resemble the hardware that connects various components in a computer. A message bus is a virtual machine with similar objectives. The main function of a bus is to distribute messages determined by a messaging protocol, and it ensures that such messages are delivered. There is not a limit on the size of the message and if it is necessary, the bus queues the messages for delivery. On the other hand, if only two servers need to communicate, the bus may allow a point-to-point connection.</p>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Advantages\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Disadvantages\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p>The applications&rsquo; complexity is reduced.</p> <p>Modifiability is more practical.</p> <p>There is a better performance since intermediaries are removed.</p> <p>Scalability is improved.</p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p>All connected parties must follow the bus conventions.</p> <p>If the bus interface is broken, the modifiability lowers.</p> <p>The security is lowered since it sends messages indiscriminately.</p> <p>The bus is the only point of failure.</p>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "modifiability"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " the ability of making changes  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It also provides modifiability just in case you need to add more components."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bind "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to link things together "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Buses provide reliable messaging capabilities to clients as they bind services from different natures."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "queue"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to organize objects that are waiting in a line "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A message bus doesn't have a limit in size and it queues the messages if necessary."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bulk "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a big amount of something  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You may use complementary shared memory techniques to manage a bulk of data. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "reliable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "trustworthy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Buses provide reliable messaging capabilities to clients as they bind services from different natures."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob11aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about message bus architecture style "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a definition for this concept "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Think about three advantages and disadvantages for using this style."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a mind map to expose your ideas about this architecture style. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your mind map with your partners.  "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search information about message bus architecture style. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a definition about message bus architecture style."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I say the advantages and disadvantages that has a message bus architecture style"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my mind map with the class."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n6le01ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<p><strong>Holly: </strong>You look puzzled. Is everything ok?</p>\n<p><strong>Ivan: </strong>Well, I am trying to connect several applications, and I need them to communicate with one another. However, if I link all the applications, there will be many point-to-point connections.</p>\n<p><strong>Holly: </strong>You may need to use a different method if you want to have a less complex connection. Why don&rsquo;t you use a message bus architecture?</p>\n<p><strong>Ivan: </strong>I&rsquo;ve heard of it, but I don&rsquo;t really understand how it works.</p>"}, {"time": "23700", "image": "enpe8n6le01ob11re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p><strong>Holly: </strong>Let me explain to you what a message bus is. It&rsquo;s a virtual machine designed to send messages among different applications. If various components or services need to interact, they will use a message bus. Buses provide reliable messaging capabilities to clients as they bind services from different natures.</p>\n<p><strong>Ivan: </strong>Is it appropriate for large amounts of data?</p>\n<p><strong>Holly: </strong>Sure. A message bus doesn&rsquo;t have a limit in size, and it queues the messages if necessary, but you may use complementary shared memory techniques to manage a bulk of data. To make sure everything is going well with your messaging bus, you just need a console client.</p>"}, {"time": "59000", "image": "enpe8n6le01ob11re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p><strong>Ivan: </strong>What advantages do I get from using this style?</p>\n<p><strong>Holly: </strong>If you use a message bus, you will reduce complexity in application communication. It also provides modifiability just in case you need to add more components. You don&rsquo;t need to use intermediary programs, and that improves performance. Finally, you may be interested in this style&rsquo;s scalability because new components don&rsquo;t affect the old ones.</p>\n<p><strong>Ivan:</strong> Are there any disadvantages?</p>\n<p><strong>Holly: </strong>Well, the communication is a little complex since all parts need to share a protocol. It also has lowered security as the messages are sent indiscriminately. If you need to change the bus interface, modifiability lowers; and finally, it has low tolerance for downtime.</p>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n6le01ob11re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe8n6le01ob11re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain what a message bus architecture is. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe the advantages of a message bus architecture. \t"}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the disadvantages of a message bus architecture."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What are the advantages of working with a software that runs several applications at the same time? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How secure do you think are systems that send messages indiscriminately to the public?  "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"